 ## Overview
-Standard-Codec-in-the-Loop (SCL) is a training framework that inserts standard, non-differentiable codecs (such as JPEG, HEVC, or AV1) directly into the neural radiance field (NeRF) training loop [S1]. It solves the problem of optimizing scene representations under realistic compression constraints by using a straight-through estimator (STE) to bypass the codec during backpropagation [S1]. Unlike prior codec-in-the-loop methods that rely on differentiable proxies or learned entropy models, SCL allows the use of arbitrary, off-the-shelf codecs [S1]. It builds on [Straight-Through Estimator (STE) for Gradient Extension](11563-straight-through-estimator-ste-for-gradient-extension.md) by applying the STE mechanism specifically to the quantization and packing steps of feature planes and density grids.
+Standard-Codec-in-the-Loop (SCL) is a training framework that inserts standard, non-differentiable codecs (such as JPEG, HEVC, or AV1) directly into the neural radiance field training loop [S1]. It solves the problem of optimizing scene representations under realistic compression constraints by using a straight-through estimator (STE) to bypass the codec during backpropagation [S1]. Unlike prior codec-in-the-loop methods that rely on differentiable proxies or learned entropy models, SCL allows the use of arbitrary, off-the-shelf codecs [S1]. It builds on [Straight-Through Estimator (STE) for Gradient Extension](11563-straight-through-estimator-ste-for-gradient-extension.md) by applying the STE mechanism specifically to the quantization and packing steps of feature planes and density grids.
 
